# Reviewed 2026-08-23 (see CI run for the full first-scan triage). Each entry
# below was individually verified against the actual image contents, not
# just accepted from the scanner - see the commit message for how.
#
# msgpack: vendored inside pip's own bundled wheel
# (/usr/local/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pip/_vendor/msgpack), not a
# package kogo or any of its declared dependencies import. Only reachable if
# pip itself ran inside the container, which it doesn't at runtime (kogo
# serve is the only thing that runs). Fix is upstream pip bundling a newer
# vendored copy, not anything in this repo.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2026-11-23

# setuptools: trivy reports this with no resolvable file path, and there is
# no setuptools package actually importable/installed in the built image
# (verified directly: `python -c "import setuptools"` fails, and no
# setuptools-named file exists anywhere in the image). Appears to be a
# metadata-detection artifact, not an installed, reachable package.
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2026-11-23

# util-linux (mount/login/libuuid1/libblkid, Debian trixie): no fix is
# available yet in the currently-pinned python:3.14-slim digest - `docker
# pull python:3.14-slim` resolves to the exact same digest already pinned in
# the Dockerfile, so there is nothing newer to re-pin to. Revisit when a
# rebuilt upstream image is published; ignore-unfixed doesn't suppress these
# because Debian's own advisory does list a fix, just not yet in this image.
CVE-2026-53612 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-53613 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-53614 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-53615 exp:2026-11-23
